<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner 9-month pre-tax profits slump.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner 9-month pre-tax profits slump.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating revenues		 39,474     vs	  21,550</p>
<p> Profit on disposal of vessel	258     vs	     568</p>
<p> Total operating revenues	 39,732     vs	  22,118</p>
<p> Operating expenses	minus  37,903     vs  minus 19,809</p>
<p> Depreciation		minus     917     vs  minus    650</p>
<p> Operating profit			912     vs	   1,659</p>
<p> Net financial items     minus	61     vs	     273</p>
<p> Profit before taxes		   851     vs	   1,932</p>
<p> Taxes			 minus     233     vs  minus    541</p>
<p> Minority interests	minus	 3     vs		 5</p>
<p> Net profit				615     vs	   1,396</p>
<p> Profit per share (crowns)	 14.17     vs	   32.13</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norwegian shipbuilder and engineering group is Kvaerner ASA. Ten Norwegian and international analysts pollede by Reuters had expected pre-tax profits of 847 million crowns for the first nine months. Kvaerner took over British conglomerate Trafalgar House in April. The results were announced in London and Oslo.</p>
<p>-Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
